wn and `S.ticks` every turn of the loop. The early manifest poll 4 s after start now happens only when the app started without a manifest or some live files failed and fell back to the snapshot; otherwise the regular poll follows at the manifest's `pollSec` (300 s now).
    - Measured, one batch, before = 3bc0488 (the bundle built at 16:10) and after = 0837fcf, same local site, interleaved. SwiftShader, 3 rounds, load 5.6 to 15.3: score 26, 26, 34 before and 34, 33, 34 after (median 26 against 34); Total Blocking Time median 22.2 s against 18.9 s (ranges 17.4 to 28.5 and 17.6 to 25.4 s, overlapping); time for the whole Lighthouse run 52.6 to 63.5 s against 40.7 to 50.0 s; of it the full-page screenshot 16.7 to 20.3 s against 9.7 to 15.1 s; the longest task 10 s or more in both (the WebGL context creation). No run in either set showed a warning that the page did not settle, and every local run completed, so the local runs do not reproduce the hosted deadline. Chrome with the Mac's GPU, 2 rounds, load 4.7 to 7.7: no change (low power stays off; medians score 46 and 46, TBT 1.99 and 1.84 s, each set with one run at FCP 2.6 s and one at 4.8 s).
    - Tests: `test/power.test.js` (the pinned renderer names, RENDERER read before the extension, the decision with software, GPU, masked and unknown names, checked to fail if the decision is made always on or always off, the keep-drawing rules, replay states, the draw schedule, the poll rule); `e2e.mjs` checks that the harness (SwiftShader) takes the low-power path with pixel ratio 1, goes idle without input (at most 3 draws in 7 s while the clock text still ticks) and wakes at once on a pointer event, and, on a page whose renderer name is made to read like a graphics card's, that low power stays off, the pixel ratio is the tier's and frames keep being drawn with no input. Results are in the commands table of `CLAUDE.md`.
    - NOT CONFIRMED: that PageSpeed Insights now completes (the owner must re-run it after a deploy); that Google's machines render in software at all; which names other software renderers give (only SwiftShader's was seen here). Phones with a slow but real GPU stay at full speed by design.
 
+15. **Embeddable live widgets and the /embed/ gallery: built on 2026-10-07 on the branch `feature/embed-widgets` (from `main` 9955550), not merged, not pushed, not deployed.** Five widgets other sites can put in an iframe: `/embed/earthquakes/` (USGS, a map of the last 24 hours with dots that pulse by magnitude, newest first), `/embed/aurora/` (NOAA SWPC Kp on a gauge with a sweeping needle and the recent three-hour periods), `/embed/tropical-storms/` (NHC's active storms turning on a map with their forecast tracks), `/embed/wildfires/` (NASA FIRMS detections as heat dots) and `/embed/tonights-sky/` (a polar chart for one of the six cities: the Moon with its phase and the five planets moving through tonight, with MET Norway's hourly cloud). Launch and ISS widgets were left out on purpose (licences not confirmed). Sources, licences, the choices that are ours and everything NOT CONFIRMED: `docs/embed-sources.md`. Code: `site/embed-models.mjs` (pure, unit tested, copied into the pages by source text like the home strip), `site/embed-widgets.mjs`, `site/embed.mjs`.
